# AppDaemon deploy playbook

Production AppDaemon runs as a custom Docker image (`ghcr.io/thaynes43/appdaemon`) in Kubernetes. App code is baked into the image at build time. Deploys happen automatically when code merges to `main`.

## How deployment works

1. Developer merges PR to `main`
2. GitHub Actions builds Docker image (`.github/workflows/build-appdaemon.yml`)
3. Image pushed to GHCR with semver tags from `VERSION` file
4. Flux detects new image and rolls the Kubernetes deployment
5. Entrypoint copies baked-in code to `/conf/apps/` and starts AppDaemon

## Versioning

- `VERSION` file at repo root = semver (e.g., `0.1.0`)
- Main: `<version>`, `<version>-<sha>`, `latest`
- Feature branches: `<branch>.<sha>`, `<branch>`

## Rules

- **Never auto-deploy**: Deployment is automatic on merge to `main`. Agents should not manually trigger deploys.
- After editing `appdaemon/**` files, tell the user what changed. Changes deploy when merged to `main`.

## Adding new Python dependencies

- Dev-only (pytest, linters): `appdaemon/requirements.txt`
- Runtime (needed in prod): `docker/requirements-prod.txt`

## Common pitfalls

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|--------|-------|-----|
| Image build fails | Bad YAML in apps-prod.yaml | Fix YAML syntax, re-push |
| Pod CrashLoopBackOff | Missing secret mounts | Check K8s secret mounts, pod logs |
| `ModuleNotFoundError` in prod | Missing dep in `docker/requirements-prod.txt` | Add dep, rebuild image |
| Old code running after merge | Flux hasn't reconciled | Check Flux status, force reconcile |
